  {
    "date": "2022-11-09",
    "term": "考える",
    "kana": "かんがえる",
    "meaning": "to think (about); to consider",
    "level": "N4",
    "pos": ["Ichidan verb", "transitive verb"],
    "priority": ["ichi1", "news1", "nf10"],
    "pitch": [4, 3],
    "stratum": "wago",
    "processes": ["derivation", "rendaku", "sound-change", "unclear"],
    "headline": "“To think” has a long run of sound changes from kamugapu, and a handful of rival theories for its start.",
    "morphemes": [],
    "sources": [
      {
        "quote": "*/kamukapu/ → /kamuɡapu/ → /kanɡafu/ → /kanɡaferu/ (regular change for lower bigrade verbs) → */kangaweru/ (semi-regular sound shift for the /f/ phoneme; see ハ行(ぎょう)転(てん)呼(こ) (ha-gyō tenko)) → /kanɡajeru/ (semi-regular sound shift, collapsing /we/ into /je/) → /kanɡaeru/"
      },
      {
        "quote": "From Old Japanese. First cited to the Nihon Shoki of 720."
      },
      {
        "quote": "Ultimate derivation uncertain. Theories include:"
      },
      {
        "quote": "* Given the ancient kamugapu spelling, may be ka + mukau, where the ka is an unidentified prefixing element, or possibly 処(か) (ka), cognate with the こ (ko) in location determiners like ここ (koko, “here”) and どこ (doko, “where”), and the mukau is 向(む)かう (mukau, “to face something, to face a direction”, pronounced as mukapu in ancient times), from the sense of facing a thing or issue to thoroughly inspect it and think it over. The shift from mukapu to mugapu may be an example of assimilation and lenition, where the preceding /m/ softens the following /k/."
      },
      {
        "quote": "* Alternatively, may be derived from the on'yomi of kan for the character 勘(かん) (kan, “intuition, perception”, prior to the development of the kana ん, this was spelled as kamu), plus some unknown element that was probably originally kapu, changing to gapu due to rendaku. The semantically relevant verbs with ancient readings of kapu, such as 変(か)える (kaeru, “to change”) all have to do with ideas of changing or turning, suggesting a possible original meaning of to change one's perception."
      },
      {
        "quote": "In addition, there are also obsolete readings of かうがふ (kaugafu, /m/ elided; compare the change of suffix む (-mu) to う (-u) or the usage of 柑(かん) (kan) in 柑(こう)子(じ) (kōji)), and かがふ (kagafu, /mu/ elided completely, as in man'yōgana or nanori usage of kanji like 安), giving further support for this etymology."
      }
    ],
    "examples": [
      {
        "id": 173469,
        "ja": "考えておくよ。",
        "en": "I'll think about it.",
        "enId": 31268,
        "form": "考えて",
        "furigana": [["考", "かんが"], ["えておくよ。"]]
      },
      {
        "id": 187506,
        "ja": "何考えてんだ？",
        "en": "Where's your head at?",
        "enId": 24643,
        "form": "考えてん",
        "furigana": [["何", "なに"], ["考", "かんが"], ["えてんだ？"]]
      }
    ],
    "wiktionaryDump": "2026-09-02"
  },
