    "term": "気配",
    "kana": "けはい",
    "meaning": "indication, sign, hint",
    "level": "N2",
    "pos": ["noun (common) (futsuumeishi)"],
    "priority": ["ichi1", "news1", "nf06"],
    "pitch": [1, 2],
    "stratum": "kango",
    "processes": ["compound", "ateji"],
    "headline": "A hint or sign is a “mood crawling around” — spelled with a 配 that was only fitted to the sound.",
    "morphemes": [],
    "sources": [
      {
        "quote": "From earlier けはひ (kefafi), a compound of 気(け) (ke, “atmosphere, spirit; feeling, mood”) + 這(は)ひ (fafi, “creeping, crawling; spreading”, modern 這(は)い (hai); the 連(れん)用(よう)形(けい) (ren'yōkei, “stem or continuative form”) of the verb 這(は)ふ (fafu, “to crawl, to creep; to spread along the ground, to spread around”, modern 這(は)う (hau)))."
